<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef prices were steady to firm on moderate to fairly strong demand and mostly moderate offerings, USDA said.  Select and Choice chuck and round cuts firm, while the rib and loin cuts generally steady. Fresh beef trimmings generally steady on light demand and offerings.</p>
<p>145 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>** 6 50s Lds 550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>28 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =	96.55	 95.61	 93.55	 91.93</p>
<p>		   0.41	  0.21	  0.94	  0.44</p>
<p>Rib	  148.19	145.09	137.14	136.78</p>
<p>Chuck	 70.41	 68.30	 73.72	 68.14</p>
<p>Round	 88.24	 88.24	 86.77	 86.77</p>
<p>Loin	 141.83	141.96	130.35	130.69</p>
<p>Brisket     61.34	 61.34	 61.35	 61.35</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  63.03	 62.97	 63.22	 63.08</p>
<p>Flank	 55.43	 55.43	 55.11	 55.11</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720)</p>
